ds), i.e. asseverate","kjv_def":"affirm constantly","n":2,"o":"1TI1:7 TIT3:8"},"G1203":{"lemma":"δεσπότης","translit":"despótēs","derivation":"perhaps from G1210 (δέω) and (a husband);","strongs_def":" an absolute ruler (\"despot\")","kjv_def":"Lord, master","n":10,"o":"LUK2:29 ACT4:24 1TI6:1 1TI6:2 2TI2:21 TIT2:9 1PE2:18 2PE2:1 JUD1:4 REV6:10"},"G1212":{"lemma":"δῆλος","translit":"dēlos","derivation":"of uncertain derivation;","strongs_def":" clear","kjv_def":"+ bewray, certain, evident, manifest","n":4,"o":"MAT26:73 1CO15:27 GAL3:11 1TI6:7"},"G1227":{"lemma":"διαβλέπω","translit":"diablépō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G991 (βλέπω);","strongs_def":" to look through, i.e. recover full vision","kjv_def":"see clearly","n":2,"o":"MAT7:5 LUK6:42"},"G1262":{"lemma":"διαλύω","translit":"dialýō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3089 (λύω);","strongs_def":" to dissolve utterly","kjv_def":"scatter","n":1,"o":"ACT5:36"},"G1283":{"lemma":"διαρπάζω","translit":"diarpázō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G726 (ἁρπάζω);","strongs_def":" to seize asunder, i.e. plunder","kjv_def":"spoil","n":2,"o":"MAT12:29 MRK3:27"},"G1275":{"lemma":"διαπαντός","translit":"diapantós","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and the genitive case of G3956 (πᾶς);","strongs_def":" through all time, i.e. (adverbially) constantly","kjv_def":"alway(-s), continually","n":7,"o":"MRK5:5 LUK24:53 ACT10:2 ACT24:16 ROM11:10 HEB9:6 HEB13:15"},"G1210":{"lemma":"δέω","translit":"déō","derivation":"a primary verb;","strongs_def":" to bind (in various applications, literally or figuratively)","kjv_def":"bind, be in bonds, knit, tie, wind","n":41,"o":"MAT12:29 MAT13:30 MAT14:3 MAT16:19 MAT18:18 MAT21:2 MAT22:13 MAT27:2 MRK3:27 MRK5:3 MRK5:4 MRK6:17 MRK11:2 MRK11:4 MRK15:1 MRK15:7 LUK13:16 LUK19:30 JHN11:44 JHN18:12 JHN18:24 JHN19:40 ACT9:2 ACT9:14 ACT9:21 ACT10:11 ACT12:6 ACT20:22 ACT21:11 ACT21:13 ACT21:33 ACT22:5 ACT22:29 ACT24:27 ROM7:2 1CO7:27 1CO7:39 COL4:3 2TI2:9 REV9:14 REV20:2"},"G1276":{"lemma":"διαπεράω