ost)","kjv_def":"second … after the first","n":1,"o":"LUK6:1"},"G1255":{"lemma":"διαλαλέω","translit":"dialaléō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G2980 (λαλέω);","strongs_def":" to talk throughout a company, i.e. converse or (genitive case) publish","kjv_def":"commune, noise abroad","n":2,"o":"LUK1:65 LUK6:11"},"G1231":{"lemma":"διαγινώσκω","translit":"diaginṓskō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G1097 (γινώσκω);","strongs_def":" to know thoroughly, i.e. ascertain exactly","kjv_def":"(would) enquire, know the uttermost","n":2,"o":"ACT23:15 ACT24:22"},"G1289":{"lemma":"διασπείρω","translit":"diaspeírō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4687 (σπείρω);","strongs_def":" to sow throughout, i.e. (figuratively) distribute in foreign lands","kjv_def":"scatter abroad","n":3,"o":"ACT8:1 ACT8:4 ACT11:19"},"G1261":{"lemma":"διαλογισμός","translit":"dialogismós","derivation":"from G1260 (διαλογίζομαι);","strongs_def":" discussion, i.e. (internal) consideration (by implication, purpose), or (external) debate","kjv_def":"dispute, doubtful(-ing), imagination, reasoning, thought","n":14,"o":"MAT15:19 MRK7:21 LUK2:35 LUK5:22 LUK6:8 LUK9:46 LUK9:47 LUK24:38 ROM1:21 ROM14:1 1CO3:20 PHP2:14 1TI2:8 JAS2:4"},"G1220":{"lemma":"δηνάριον","translit":"dēnárion","derivation":"of Latin origin;","strongs_def":" a denarius (or ten asses)","kjv_def":"pence, penny(-worth)","n":15,"o":"MAT18:28 MAT20:2 MAT20:9 MAT20:10 MAT20:13 MAT22:19 MRK6:37 MRK12:15 MRK14:5 LUK7:41 LUK10:35 LUK20:24 JHN6:7 JHN12:5 REV6:6"},"G1257":{"lemma":"διαλείπω","translit":"dialeípō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3007 (λείπω);","strongs_def":" to leave off in the middle, i.e. intermit","kjv_def":"cease","n":1,"o":"LUK7:45"},"G1299":{"lemma":"διατάσσω","translit":"diatássō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G5021 (τάσσω);","strongs_def":" to arrange thoroughly, i.e. (specially) institute, prescribe, etc.","kjv_def":"appoint, command, give, (set in) order, ordain","n":16,"o":"MAT11:1 LUK3:13 LUK8:55 LUK17:9 LUK17:10 ACT7:44 ACT18:2 ACT20:13 ACT23:31 ACT24:23 1CO7:17 1CO9:14 1CO11:34 1CO16:1 GAL3:19 TIT1:5"},"G1242":{"lemma":"διαθήκη","translit":"diathḗkē","derivation":"from G1303 (διατίθεμαι);","strongs_def":" properly, a disposition, i.e. (specially) a contract (especially a devisory will)","kjv_def":"covenant, testament","n":30,"o":"MAT26:28 MRK14:24 LUK1:72 LUK22:20 ACT3:25 ACT7:8 ROM9:4 ROM11:27 1CO11:25 2CO3:6 2CO3:14 GAL3:15 GAL3:17 GAL4:24 EPH2:12 HEB7:22 HEB8:6 HEB8:8 HEB8:9 HEB8:10 HEB9:4 HEB9:15 HEB9:16 HEB9:17 HEB9:20 HEB10:16 HEB10:29 HEB12:24 HEB13:20 REV11:19"},"G1269":{"lemma":"διανεύω","translit":"dianeúō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3506 (νεύω);","strongs_def":" to nod (or express by signs) across an intervening space","kjv_def":"beckon","n":1,"o":"LUK1:22"},"G1232":{"lemma":"διαγνωρίζω","translit":"diagnōrízō","derivation":"from G1123 (γραπτός) and G1107 (γνωρίζω);","strongs_def":" to tell abroad","kjv_def":"make known","n":1,"o":"LUK2:17"},"G1252":{"lemma":"διακρίνω","translit":"diakrínō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G2919 (κρίνω);","strongs_def":" to separate thoroughly, i.e. (literally and reflexively) to withdraw from, or (by implication) oppose; figuratively, to discriminate (by implication, decide), or (reflexively) hesitate","kjv_def":"contend, make (to) differ(-ence), discern, doubt, judge, be partial, stagger, waver","n":18,"o":"MAT16:3 MAT21:21 MRK11:23 ACT10:20 ACT11:2 ACT11:12 ACT15:9 ROM4:20 ROM14:23 1CO4:7 1CO6:5 1CO11:29 1CO11:31 1CO14:29 JAS1:6 JAS2:4 JUD1:9 JUD1:22"},"G1205":{"lemma":"δεῦτε","translit":"deûte","derivation":"from G1204 (δεῦρο) and an imperative form of (to go);","strongs_def":" come hither!","kjv_def":"come, X follow","n":13,"o":"MAT4:19 MAT11:28 MAT21:38 MAT22:4 MAT25:34 MAT28:6 MRK1:17 MRK6:31 MRK12:7 LUK20:14 JHN4:29 JHN21:12 REV19:17"},"G1236":{"lemma":"διάγω","translit":"diágō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G71 (ἄγω);","strongs_def":" to pass time or life","kjv_def":"lead life, living","n":2,"o":"1TI2:2 TIT3:3"},"G1271":{"lemma":"διάνοια","translit":"diánoia","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3563 (νοῦς);","strongs_def":" deep thought, properly, the faculty (mind or its disposition), by implication, its exercise","kjv_def":" imagination, mind, understanding","n":13,"o":"MAT22:37 MRK12:30 LUK1:51 LUK10:27 EPH1:18 EPH2:3 EPH4:18 COL1:21 HEB8:10 HEB10:16 1PE1:13 2PE3:1 1JN5:20"},"G1206":{"lemma":"δευτεραῖος","translit":"deuteraîos","derivation":"from G1208 (δεύτερος);","strongs_def":" secondary, i.e. (specially) on the second day","kjv_def":"next day","n":1,"o":"ACT28:13"},"G1237":{"lemma":"διαδέχομαι","translit":"diadéchomai","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G1209 (δέχομαι);","strongs_def":" to receive in turn, i.e. (figuratively) succeed to","kjv_def":"come after","n":1,"o":"ACT7:45"},"G1294":{"lemma":"διαστρέφω","translit":"diastréphō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4762 (στρέφω);","strongs_def":" to distort, i.e. (figuratively) misinterpret, or (morally) corrupt","kjv_def":"perverse(-rt), turn away","n":7,"o":"MAT17:17 LUK9:41 LUK23:2 ACT13:8 ACT13:10 ACT20:30 PHP2:15"},"G1264":{"lemma":"διαμάχομαι","translit":"diamáchomai","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3164 (μάχομαι);","strongs_def":" to fight fiercely (in altercation)","kjv_def":"strive","n":1,"o":"ACT23:9"},"G1204":{"lemma":"δεῦρο","translit":"deûro","derivation":"of uncertain affinity;","strongs_def":" here; used also imperative hither!; and of time, hitherto","kjv_def":"come (hither), hither(-to)","n":8,"o":"MAT19:21 MRK10:21 LUK18:22 JHN11:43 ACT7:3 ACT7:34 REV17:1 REV21:9"},"G1286":{"lemma":"διασείω","translit":"diaseíō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4579 (σείω);","strongs_def":" to shake thoroughly, i.e. (figuratively) to intimidate","kjv_def":"do violence to","n":1,"o":"LUK3:14"},"G1267":{"lemma":"διαμερισμός","translit":"diamerismós","derivation":"from G1266 (διαμερίζω);","strongs_def":" disunion (of opinion and conduct)","kjv_def":"division","n":1,"o":"LUK12:51"},"G1281":{"lemma":"διαπραγματεύομαι","translit":"diapragmateúomai","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4231 (πραγματεύομαι);","strongs_def":" to thoroughly occupy oneself, i.e. (transitively and by implication) to earn in business","kjv_def":"gain by trading","n":1,"o":"LUK19:15"},"G1278":{"lemma":"διαπονέω","translit":"diaponéō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and a derivative of G4192 (πόνος);","strongs_def":" to toil through, i.e. (passively) be worried","kjv_def":"be grieved","n":2,"o":"ACT4:2 ACT16:18"},"G1230":{"lemma":"διαγίνομαι","translit":"diagínomai","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G1096 (γίνομαι);","strongs_def":" to elapse meanwhile","kjv_def":"X after, be past, be spent","n":3,"o":"MRK16:1 ACT25:13 ACT27:9"},"G1244":{"lemma":"διαιρέω","translit":"diairéō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G138 (αἱρέομαι);","strongs_def":" to separate, i.e. distribute","kjv_def":"divide","n":2,"o":"LUK15:12 1CO12:11"},"G1202":{"lemma":"δεσμώτης","translit":"desmṓtēs","derivation":"from the same as G1201 (δεσμωτήριον);","strongs_def":" (passively) a captive","kjv_def":"prisoner","n":2,"o":"ACT27:1 ACT27:42"},"G1295":{"lemma":"διασώζω","translit":"diasṓzō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4982 (σώζω);","strongs_def":" to save thoroughly, i.e. (by implication or analogy) to cure, preserve, rescue, etc.","kjv_def":"bring safe, escape (safe), heal, make perfectly whole, save","n":8,"o":"MAT14:36 LUK7:3 ACT23:24 ACT27:43 ACT27:44 ACT28:1 ACT28:4 1PE3:20"},"G1201":{"lemma":"δεσμωτήριον","translit":"desmōtḗrion","derivation":"from a derivative of G1199 (δεσμόν) (equivalent to G1196 (δεσμέω));","strongs_def":" a place of bondage, i.e. a dungeon","kjv_def":"prison","n":4,"o":"MAT11:2 ACT5:21 ACT5:23 ACT16:26"},"G1265":{"lemma":"διαμένω","translit":"diaménō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3306 (μένω);","strongs_def":" to stay constantly (in being or relation)","kjv_def":"continue, remain","n":5,"o":"LUK1:22 LUK22:28 GAL2:5 HEB1:11 2PE3:4"},"G1223":{"lemma":"διά","translit":"diá","deriv