ch was (give) commanded(-ment)","n":7,"o":"MAT16:20 MRK5:43 MRK7:36 MRK8:15 MRK9:9 ACT15:24 HEB12:20"},"G1288":{"lemma":"διασπάω","translit":"diaspáō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4685 (σπάω);","strongs_def":" to draw apart, i.e. sever or dismember","kjv_def":"pluck asunder, pull in pieces","n":2,"o":"MRK5:4 ACT23:10"},"G1290":{"lemma":"διασπορά","translit":"diasporá","derivation":"from G1289 (διασπείρω);","strongs_def":" dispersion, i.e. (specially and concretely) the (converted) Israelite resident in Gentile countries","kjv_def":"(which are) scattered (abroad)","n":3,"o":"JHN7:35 JAS1:1 1PE1:1"},"G1263":{"lemma":"διαμαρτύρομαι","translit":"diamartýromai","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G3140 (μαρτυρέω);","strongs_def":" to attest or protest earnestly, or (by implication) hortatively","kjv_def":"charge, testify (unto), witness","n":15,"o":"LUK16:28 ACT2:40 ACT8:25 ACT10:42 ACT18:5 ACT20:21 ACT20:23 ACT20:24 ACT23:11 ACT28:23 1TH4:6 1TI5:21 2TI2:14 2TI4:1 HEB2:6"},"G1280":{"lemma":"διαπορέω","translit":"diaporéō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G639 (ἀπορέω);","strongs_def":" to be thoroughly nonplussed","kjv_def":"(be in) doubt, be (much) perplexed","n":5,"o":"LUK9:7 LUK24:4 ACT2:12 ACT5:24 ACT10:17"},"G1284":{"lemma":"διαῤῥήσσω","translit":"diarrhḗssō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G4486 (ῥήγνυμι);","strongs_def":" to tear asunder","kjv_def":"break, rend","n":5,"o":"MAT26:65 MRK14:63 LUK5:6 LUK8:29 ACT14:14"},"G1214":{"lemma":"Δημᾶς","translit":"Dēmâs","derivation":"probably for G1216 (Δημήτριος);","strongs_def":" Demas, a Christian","kjv_def":"Demas","n":3,"o":"COL4:14 2TI4:10 PHM1:24"},"G1298":{"lemma":"διαταράσσω","translit":"diatarássō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G5015 (ταράσσω);","strongs_def":" to disturb wholly, i.e. agitate (with alarm)","kjv_def":"trouble","n":1,"o":"LUK1:29"}}